4
01:20:02,142 --> 01:20:12,857
In heart failure, we still recommend not to prescribe, but that's something that is still in debate and probably will have more results on that in the future.

5
01:20:12,857 --> 01:20:23,571
But at this point, if you have a patient with heart failure risk, you should not recommend pioglitazone.

6
01:20:23,571 --> 01:20:34,285
And I want to just remind you that in the major study for three years with pioglitazone, no major safety concerns were observed in that trial.

7
01:20:34,285 --> 01:20:45,000
Besides that, I'm talking about the benefits of pioglitazone for MSLD, but actually there are several other benefits of pioglitazone in terms of cardiovascular and cardiometabolic disorders.

8
01:20:45,000 --> 01:20:55,714
So even though it causes weight gain, actually there is a fat redistribution that is well described and reverses lipotoxicity.

9
01:20:55,714 --> 01:21:06,428
But at the same time, you have improvement in hyperglycemia, the lowering of the A1C is actually durable, and usually when we look at those trials that you see improvement in A1C and with time the A1C starts going up, this is much less notable in patients taking pioglitazone.

10
01:21:06,428 --> 01:21:17,142
There's improvement in insulin resistance, improvement in lipid profile with decreasing triglycerides, increasing HDL, improves also endothelial function and inflammation.

11
01:21:17,142 --> 01:21:27,857
And there are some also, you know, do we have good data showing pioglitazone has some cardiovascular benefit? And actually we do.

12
01:21:27,857 --> 01:21:38,571
The PROACTIVE study and IRIS studies actually show there was a reduction in secondary prevention for both MI and stroke.

13
01:21:38,571 --> 01:21:49,285
So in overall, it's a good drug in terms not just diabetes control and methyl D, but as mentioned before, methyl D is associated with cardiovascular disease and this is a drug that can have other benefits.

14
01:21:49,285 --> 01:22:00,000
The question of liver fibrosis is still in the air for the pioglitazone studies, but I just want to mention this meta-analysis that was performed in 2017, combined some of the studies that I mentioned before.

15
01:22:00,000 --> 01:22:10,714
And actually they saw the combined all the studies together, there is actually an improvement in advanced fibrosis.

16
01:22:10,714 --> 01:22:21,428
And there's this recent meta-analysis in 2025, in February, actually when they compare several of the studies that published, although they do not have some of the most recent study that we're showing here today, but they actually saw that pioglitazone was one of the best benefits in terms of NASH resolution without worsening fibrosis and a more than equal or more two-point decrease in FOD activity score.

17
01:22:21,428 --> 01:22:32,142
So now the question is, does combination therapy with pioglitazone has beneficial effect to muscle D? So I want to go over, so there are no good long-term studies showing that, but I want to go over this study with, there was the triple therapy from the San Antonio group.

18
01:22:32,142 --> 01:22:42,857
And in this study, they randomized, they had 68 patients and they randomized some for triple therapy with metformin, xenotide, and pioglitazone against a control group that used exemplified conventional therapy with metformin, glycoside, and insulin.

19
01:22:42,857 --> 01:22:53,571
And in this study, on the top figure, you can see A1C, it was lower within the first few months, and you can see the A1C remained much lower with the triple therapy study.

20
01:22:53,571 --> 01:23:04,285
This study was not focused on treatment of patients with MEFOD, but they evaluate patients who had diabetes.

21
01:23:04,285 --> 01:23:15,000
And so you can see here in the conventional therapy, ALT, AST, they did not reduce with treatment, but actually ALT levels were much higher at the end of the study.

22
01:23:15,000 --> 01:23:25,714
And while the triple therapy, you see there was a significant decrease in both ALT and AST, and they remained stable until the end of the study.

23
01:23:25,714 --> 01:23:36,428
So there was a change in body weight, but it was not significant with the two groups, suggesting that combination with pioglitazone could be a way to mitigate some of the weight gain effects from pioglitazone.

24
01:23:36,428 --> 01:23:47,142
And they didn't have a baseline study with FibroScan, but they measured FibroScan at the end of the study, and actually steatosis was 31% in patients in the triple therapy compared to 69% in the conventional group.

25
01:23:47,142 --> 01:23:57,857
And fibrosis measured also with FibroScan was 7% in the triple therapy group and 26% in the conventional group, as some promising results then.

26
01:23:57,857 --> 01:24:08,571
So just to go over the MEFOD consensus from the American Diabetes Association was just released in June 2025, and I want to mention here that pioglitazone is still listed there as a treatment option and also together with GLP-1s and SGLT2 inhibitors as mentioned in the, you know, with all the data that we saw here before.

27
01:24:08,571 --> 01:24:19,285
So in summary and next steps, pioglitazone improves the steatosis and necroinflammation in patients with MASH.

28
01:24:19,285 --> 01:24:30,000
Long-term studies show to be safe and have additional cardiovascular benefits.

29
01:24:30,000 --> 01:24:40,714
Future studies will be important to define the benefit of combination therapy with pioglitazone.

30
01:24:40,714 --> 01:24:51,428
And also there are some newer PPARs receptor agonists, and we'll see in the near future we might have some more results on that.

